: 'call_8d1c813f1ed445658369e33f', 'content': '{\n  "content": "  1| from __future__ import annotations\\n  2| import random\\n  3| import numpy as np\\n  4| \\n  5| def select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]:\\n  6|     \\"\\"\\"\\n  7|     Selection policy for Project-BDA.\\n  8| \\n  9|     Contract (MUST KEEP EXACTLY):\\n 10|         select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]\\n 11| \\n 12|     Inputs:\\n 13|     - candidates: list[dict]\\n 14|         - single-gene datasets: each item includes {\\"gene\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 15|         - gene-pair datasets: each item includes {\\"gene_a\\": \\"<HGNC>\\", \\"gene_b\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 16|         - gene search (optional): when enabled by the runner, you may call:\\n 17|           - import bda_tools\\n 18|           - bda_tools.gene_search(query_gene: str, k: int = 10, diverse: bool = False) -> list[int]\\n 19|     - history: list[dict]\\n 20|         - each item includes at least:\\n 21|           - candidate_index: int\\n 22|           - score: float\\n 23|           - hit: int (0/1) if enabled by runner\\n 24|     - batch_size: int\\n 25|     - seed: int\\n 26| \\n 27|     Output:\\n 28|     - list[int] of NEW candidate indices (no repeats; already-selected may be ignored/replaced by runner).\\n 29|     \\n 30|     Strategy: Hybrid exploration-exploitation with adaptive sampling\\n 31|     - Early rounds: More random exploration to discover promising regions\\n 32|     - Later rounds: More exploitation of high-scoring candidates\\n 33|     - Always maintain diversity to avoid getting stuck in local optima\\n 34|     \\"\\"\\"\\n 35|     rng = random.Random(seed)\\n 36|     \\n 37|     # Get already selected indices\\n 38|     selected = set(h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history)\\n 39|     \\n 40|     # Get all available candidate indices\\n 41|     all_indices = list(range(len(candidates)))\\n 42|     available = [i for i in all_indices if i not in selected]\\n 43|     \\n 44|     if len(available) <= batch_size:\\n 45|         return available\\n 46|     \\n 47|     # Calculate exploration ratio based on history size\\n 48|     # More exploration in early rounds, more exploitation later\\n 49|     num_rounds = len(history) // batch_size if batch_size > 0 else 0\\n 50|     exploration_ratio = max(0.2, 0.9 - 0.15 * num_rounds)  # Starts at 90%, decreases to 20%\\n 51|     \\n 52|     # Separate exploration and exploitation\\n 53|     num_explore = int(batch_size * exploration_ratio)\\n 54|     num_exploit = batch_size - num_explore\\n 55|     \\n 56|     # Exploration: random sampling from available candidates\\n 57|     explore_indices = rng.sample(available, min(num_explore, len(available)))\\n 58|     \\n 59|     # Exploitation: select based on historical scores\\n 60|     if len(history) > 0 and num_exploit > 0:\\n 61|         # Sort by absolute score to prioritize both negative and positive extremes\\n 62|         sorted_history = sorted(history, key=lambda x: abs(x[\'score\']), reverse=True)\\n 63|         \\n 64|         # Get top performers (highest absolute scores, 20% or at least 10)\\n 65|         top_k = max(10, len(sorted_history) // 5)\\n 66|         top_performers = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in sorted_history[:top_k]]\\n 67|         \\n 68|         # Find candidates similar to top performers if gene search is available\\n 69|         exploit_candidates = set()\\n 70|         remaining_avail = [i for i in available if i not in explore_indices]\\n 71|         \\n 72|         if len(remaining_avail) > 0:\\n 73|             # Try to use gene search if available\\n 74|             try:\\n 75|                 import bda_tools\\n 76|                 # Sample from top performers and find similar genes\\n 77|                 num_to_sample = min(5, len(top_performers))\\n 78|                 sampled_top = rng.sample(top_performers, num_to_sample)\\n 79|                 \\n 80|                 for top_idx in sampled_top:\\n 81|                     if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n 82|                         break\\n 83|                     # Get gene name from candidate\\n 84|                     candidate = candidates[top_idx]\\n 85|                     gene = candidate.get(\'gene\') or candidate.get(\'gene_a\')\\n 86|                     if gene:\\n 87|                         try:\\n 88|                             similar = bda_tools.gene_search(gene, k=min(20, num_exploit), diverse=False)\\n 89|                             for idx in similar:\\n 90|                                 if idx in remaining_avail and idx not in exploit_candidates:\\n 91|                                     exploit_candidates.add(idx)\\n 92|                                     if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n 93|                                         break\\n 94|                         except:\\n 95|                             pass\\n 96|             except ImportError:\\n 97|                 # bda_tools not available, fall back to other strategies\\n 98|                 pass\\n 99|             \\n100|             # If we still need more candidates, use weighted sampling\\n101|             if len(exploit_candidates) < num_exploit:\\n102|                 needed = num_exploit - len(exploit_candidates)\\n103|                 # Use stratified sampling for diversity: divide remaining into buckets\\n104|                 num_buckets = min(10, len(remaining_avail))\\n105|                 bucket_size = len(remaining_avail) // num_buckets\\n106|                 \\n107|                 sampled = set()\\n108|                 for bucket in range(num_buckets):\\n109|                     if len(sampled) >= needed:\\n110|                         break\\n111|                     start = bucket * bucket_size\\n112|                     end = start + bucket_size if bucket < num_buckets - 1 else len(remaining_avail)\\n113|                     bucket_items = remaining_avail[start:end]\\n114|                     if bucket_items:\\n115|                         sampled.add(rng.choice(bucket_items))\\n116|                 \\n117|                 exploit_candidates.update(sampled)\\n118|         \\n119|         selected_indices = list(explore_indices) + list(exploit_candidates)[:num_exploit]\\n120|     else:\\n121|         # Pure exploration if no history or no exploitation needed\\n122|         selected_indices = explore_indices\\n123|     \\n124|     # Ensure we have exactly batch_size indices\\n125|     if len(selected_indices) < batch_size:\\n126|         remaining = [i for i in available if i not in selected_indices]\\n127|         needed = batch_size - len(selected_indices)\\n128|         if remaining:\\n129|             selected_indices.extend(rng.sample(remaining, min(needed, len(remaining))))\\n130|     \\n131|     return selected_indices[:batch_size]"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Now I'll make my targeted improvement. The key insight is that hits show a bimodal distribution (very negative AND near-zero scores). I'll improve the exploitation strategy to better target both modes:\n", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_49b066e5c06943c1a31f831f', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'replace', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21/run-1/candidates/candidate_4/harness/model.py", "instruction": "Improve exploitation strategy to better target bimodal hit distribution (very negative and near-zero scores). When hit information is available, prioritize genes similar to actual hits. Increase gene search sampling and add diverse search for better coverage.", "old_string": "        # Find candidates similar to top performers if gene search is available\\n        exploit_candidates = set()\\n        remaining_avail = [i for i in available if i not in explore_indices]\\n        \\n        if len(remaining_avail) > 0:\\n            # Try to use gene search if available\\n            try:\\n                import bda_tools\\n                # Sample from top performers and find similar genes\\n                num_to_sample = min(5, len(top_performers))\\n                sampled_top = rng.sample(top_performers, num_to_sample)\\n                \\n                for top_idx in sampled_top:\\n                    if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n                        break\\n                    # Get gene name from candidate\\n                    candidate = candidates[top_idx]\\n                    gene = candidate.get(\'gene\') or candidate.get(\'gene_a\')\\n                    if gene:\\n                        try:\\n                            similar = bda_tools.gene_search(gene, k=min(20, num_exploit), diverse=False)\\n                            for idx in similar:\\n                                if idx in remaining_avail and idx not in exploit_candidates:\\n                                    exploit_candidates.add(idx)\\n                                    if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n                                        break\\n                        except:\\n                            pass\\n            except ImportError:\\n                # bda_tools not available, fall back to other strategies\\n                pass\\n            \\n            # If we still need more candidates, use weighted sampling\\n            if len(exploit_candidates) < num_exploit:\\n                needed = num_exploit - len(exploit_candidates)\\n                # Use stratified sampling for diversity: divide remaining into buckets\\n                num_buckets = min(10, len(remaining_avail))\\n                bucket_size = len(remaining_avail) // num_buckets\\n                \\n                sampled = set()\\n                for bucket in range(num_buckets):\\n                    if len(sampled) >= needed:\\n                        break\\n                    start = bucket * bucket_size\\n                    end = start + bucket_size if bucket < num_buckets - 1 else len(remaining_avail)\\n                    bucket_items = remaining_avail[start:end]\\n                    if bucket_items:\\n                        sampled.add(rng.choice(bucket_items))\\n                \\n                exploit_candidates.update(sampled)", "new_string": "        # Find candidates similar to top performers if gene search is available\\n        exploit_candidates = set()\\n        remaining_avail = [i for i in available if i not in explore_indices]\\n        \\n        if len(remaining_avail) > 0:\\n            # Try to use gene search if available\\n            try:\\n                import bda_tools\\n                \\n                # If hit information is available, prioritize actual hits over just high absolute scores\\n                if any(\'hit\' in h for h in history):\\n                    hit_indices = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history if h.get(\'hit\') == 1]\\n                    if hit_indices:\\n                        # Prioritize genes that are actual hits\\n                        top_performers = hit_indices[:min(len(hit_indices), top_k)]\\n                \\n                # Sample more aggressively from top performers\\n                num_to_sample = min(10, len(top_performers))\\n                sampled_top = rng.sample(top_performers, num_to_sample)\\n                \\n                for top_idx in sampled_top:\\n                    if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n                        break\\n                    # Get gene name from candidate\\n                    candidate = candidates[top_idx]\\n                    gene = candidate.get(\'gene\') or candidate.get(\'gene_a\')\\n                    if gene:\\n                        try:\\n                            # Search for similar genes with higher k\\n                            similar = bda_tools.gene_search(gene, k=min(30, num_exploit * 2), diverse=False)\\n                            for idx in similar:\\n                                if idx in remaining_avail and idx not in exploit_candidates:\\n                                    exploit_candidates.add(idx)\\n                                    if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n                                        break\\n                        except:\\n                            pass\\n                \\n                # If we still need candidates, also try diverse search around top performers\\n                if len(exploit_candidates) < num_exploit:\\n                    for top_idx in sampled_top:\\n                        if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n                            break\\n                        candidate = candidates[top_idx]\\n                        gene = candidate.get(\'gene\') or candidate.get(\'gene_a\')\\n                        if gene:\\n                            try:\\n                                # Try diverse search for broader coverage\\n                                diverse_similar = bda_tools.gene_search(gene, k=min(20, num_exploit - len(exploit_candidates)), diverse=True)\\n                                for idx in diverse_similar:\\n                                    if idx in remaining_avail and idx not in exploit_candidates:\\n                                        exploit_candidates.add(idx)\\n                                        if len(exploit_candidates) >= num_exploit:\\n                                            break\\n                            except:\\n                                pass\\n            except ImportError:\\n                # bda_tools not available, fall back to other strategies\\n                pass\\n            \\n            # If we still need more candidates, use weighted sampling based on score patterns\\n            if len(exploit_candidates) < num_exploit:\\n                needed = num_exploit - len(exploit_candidates)\\n                \\n                # Analyze score distribution to target both extremes\\n                scores = [h[\'score\'] for h in history]\\n                if scores:\\n                    # Target both very negative and near-zero regions\\n                    extreme_negative = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history if h[\'score\'] < -2.0]\\n                    near_zero = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history if abs(h[\'score\']) < 0.1]\\n                    \\n                    # Sample from both regions if available\\n                    if extreme_negative and needed > 1:\\n                        idx = rng.choice(extreme_negative)\\n                        if idx in remaining_avail and idx not in exploit_candidates:\\n                            exploit_candidates.add(idx)\\n                            needed -= 1\\n                    \\n                    if near_zero and needed > 0:\\n                        idx = rng.choice(near_zero)\\n                        if idx in remaining_avail and idx not in exploit_candidates:\\n                            exploit_candidates.add(idx)\\n                            needed -= 1\\n                \\n                # Use stratified sampling for remaining diversity\\n                if needed > 0:\\n                    num_buckets = min(10, len(remaining_avail))\\n                    bucket_size = len(remaining_avail) // num_buckets\\n                    \\n                    sampled = set()\\n                    for bucket in range(num_buckets):\\n                        if len(sampled) >= needed:\\n                            break\\n                        start = bucket * bucket_size\\n                        end = start + bucket_size if bucket < num_buckets - 1 else len(remaining_avail)\\n                        bucket_items = remaining_avail[start:end]\\n                        if bucket_items:\\n                            sampled.add(rng.choice(bucket_items))\\n                    \\n                    exploit_candidates.update(sampled)"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_49b066e5c06943c1a31f831f', 'content': '{\n  "content": "Successfully modified file: /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21/run-1/candidates/candidate_4/harness/model.py (1 replacements, strategy: exact)."\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now let me write the reasoning document:\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_1ebe34bfda7842168270afb1', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'write_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21/run-1/candidates/candidate_4/proposer_reasoning.md", "content": "# Proposer Reasoning - Candidate 4\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\nModified the exploitation strategy in `model.py` to better target the bimodal hit distribution observed in the Sanchez21 dataset:\\n\\n1. **Hit-Prioritized Sampling**: When hit information is available in history, the model now prioritizes actual hits over just high absolute scores for gene search.\\n\\n2. **More Aggressive Gene Search**: Increased sampling from top performers (5 → 10 genes) and increased search depth (k=20 → k=30) to find more similar candidates.\\n\\n3. **Diverse Search Fallback**: Added a second-pass diverse gene search when similar gene search doesn\'t yield enough candidates, providing broader coverage.\\n\\n4. **Bimodal Targeting**: Added explicit targeting of both extreme negative scores (< -2.0) and near-zero scores (< 0.1) in the fallback sampling strategy, matching the observed hit distribution.\\n\\n## Why This Is Better\\n\\n**Evidence from History:**\\n- Candidate 1 → 2: Sorting by lowest scores improved hits from 8 to 15\\n- Candidate 2 → 3: Sorting by absolute scores improved hits from 15 to 18\\n- However, round 3 precision dropped to 2.34%, suggesting the absolute score approach wasn\'t effectively exploiting discoveries\\n\\n**Hit Distribution Analysis:**\\nThe 18 hits show a bimodal pattern:\\n- Extreme negatives: -4.21, -3.40, -3.35, -3.12, -3.09, -2.69, -2.68\\n- Near-zero: -0.10, -0.085, -0.084, -0.067, -0.048, -0.043, -0.037, -0.031, -0.027, -0.007\\n\\nThe current absolute score approach treats both extremes equally but doesn\'t effectively use the hit label or gene search to find similar candidates.\\n\\n## Expected Impact\\n\\nThis change should:\\n1. **Increase hit rate**: Better targeting of both hit modes should improve precision in later rounds\\n2. **Better exploitation**: More aggressive gene search around actual hits should find more promising candidates\\n3. **Maintain diversity**: Diverse search fallback prevents over-concentration in one region\\n4. **Conservative improvement**: This is a targeted refinement of the existing strategy, not a risky rewrite\\n\\nThe modification is low-risk because it builds on the proven absolute score approach while adding better hit utilization and more comprehensive gene search."}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_1ebe34bfda7842168270afb1', 'content': '{\n  "content": "Successfully created and wrote to new file: /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21/run-1/candidates/candidate_4/proposer_reasoning.md."\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Let me verify the syntax of the modified model:\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_8b8730e8f66d4e97a8584b62', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'run_shell_command', 'arguments': '{"command": "cd /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21/run-1/candidates/candidate_4/harness && python3 -m py_compile model.py && echo \\"Syntax OK\\"", "description": "Verify Python syntax